module Signals

# ============================================================================
# Current-process signal handlers.
#
# Register a handler to run when the OS asks this process to stop:
#   - `when_interrupted` — the user interrupted it (Ctrl-C / SIGINT).
#   - `when_terminated`  — the OS is terminating it (SIGTERM / console-close).
#
# Registering a handler SUPPRESSES the default termination: the process no longer
# dies on its own, and YOUR handler decides what to do (typically: flip a flag your
# main loop polls, then exit). Handlers run on a dedicated dispatch thread, NOT the
# main thread, so keep them small (set a flag, log, save) and do not assume they run
# in main-thread context.
#
# The handler is a bare routine value — pass a named `routine on_stop()` by name
# (RazorForge lambdas are expression-only, so a multi-statement handler must be a
# named routine). Any state the handler touches must outlive the process (module
# state / a `Retained` handle it can reach), since it may fire at any time.
#
# NOTE: SIGKILL and the OOM-killer cannot be caught — the process dies before any
# handler runs. `when_terminated` covers the catchable termination request (SIGTERM),
# not a forced kill.
# ============================================================================

### Registers a handler to run when the process is interrupted (Ctrl-C / SIGINT).
### Registering SUPPRESSES the default termination — the handler decides whether to
### exit. Multiple handlers may be registered; all run, in registration order, on a
### dedicated dispatch thread.
### :param handler: A `() -> None` routine to run on interrupt.
routine when_interrupted(handler: Routine[(), None])
  danger
    C::rf_signal_register(0_s32, handler)
  return

### Registers a handler to run when the process is terminated (SIGTERM / console-close).
### Registering SUPPRESSES the default termination — the handler decides whether to
### exit. Multiple handlers may be registered; all run, in registration order, on a
### dedicated dispatch thread. A forced kill (SIGKILL / OOM-killer) cannot be caught.
### :param handler: A `() -> None` routine to run on termination.
routine when_terminated(handler: Routine[(), None])
  danger
    C::rf_signal_register(1_s32, handler)
  return

# ============================================================================
# Context overloads — carry shared state to the handler.
#
# The handler runs on the dispatch thread, so the state it touches must be a
# thread-safe, storable handle: a `Guarded[T, P]` (RazorForge's multi-thread RC) or a
# `Roamed[T]` (Suflae's auto-promoting entity handle). The registration RETAINS the
# handle for the process lifetime (a Roamed context is also promoted to its atomic
# escaped mode, since another thread now reaches it), so the state stays alive and
# access stays serialized. The handler receives the same handle back on every fire —
# no capture, no global; state flows through an explicit owned handle.
# ============================================================================

### Interrupt handler carrying a `Guarded[T, P]` context (RazorForge multi-thread state).
routine when_interrupted[T, P](handler: Routine[(Guarded[T, P],), None], context: Guarded[T, P])
needs EntityType T, P obeys LockPolicy
  danger
    Hijacked[GuardController[T, P]](context).as_entity().hold()
    C::rf_signal_register_ctx(0_s32,
      Hijacked[Byte](handler).get_address(),
      Hijacked[GuardController[T, P]](context).get_address())
  return

### Termination handler carrying a `Guarded[T, P]` context (RazorForge multi-thread state).
routine when_terminated[T, P](handler: Routine[(Guarded[T, P],), None], context: Guarded[T, P])
needs EntityType T, P obeys LockPolicy
  danger
    Hijacked[GuardController[T, P]](context).as_entity().hold()
    C::rf_signal_register_ctx(1_s32,
      Hijacked[Byte](handler).get_address(),
      Hijacked[GuardController[T, P]](context).get_address())
  return

### Interrupt handler carrying a `Roamed[T]` context (Suflae entity state).
routine when_interrupted[T](handler: Routine[(Roamed[T],), None], context: Roamed[T])
needs EntityType T
  danger
    var ctrl = Hijacked[RoamController[T]](context).as_entity()
    ctrl.promote()
    ctrl.hold()
    C::rf_signal_register_ctx(0_s32,
      Hijacked[Byte](handler).get_address(),
      Hijacked[RoamController[T]](context).get_address())
  return

### Termination handler carrying a `Roamed[T]` context (Suflae entity state).
routine when_terminated[T](handler: Routine[(Roamed[T],), None], context: Roamed[T])
needs EntityType T
  danger
    var ctrl = Hijacked[RoamController[T]](context).as_entity()
    ctrl.promote()
    ctrl.hold()
    C::rf_signal_register_ctx(1_s32,
      Hijacked[Byte](handler).get_address(),
      Hijacked[RoamController[T]](context).get_address())
  return
